 to build the stage.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: That stage is so large, it`s hard to fathom. More than 80 percent of Americans say they use \uc2 YouTube\uc2 , a searchable buffet of not just Americans, but humanity`s many talents and interests, from ant farms to ziplining, watched for 194 hours a year by the average user.\par \par \uc2 And walking through the company`s offices in New York, it`s hard to imagine this $29 billion a year business began with a single grainy upload.\par \par \uc2 You recognize this video?\par \par \uc2 NEAL MOHAN: Yes.\par \par \uc2 MAN: Cool thing about these guys is that they have really, really, really long tusks.\par \par \uc2 NEAL MOHAN: You know, I`ve watched this video, at least dozens and dozens of times. And every time I watch it, it gives me goosebumps because it reminds me of where \uc2 YouTube\uc2  came from.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: So what has \uc2 YouTube\uc2  become? What is \uc2 YouTube\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 NEAL MOHAN: You know, in some senses, we are exactly the same as where that video started, we are a place where our objective, our mission is to give everyone a voice and show them the world.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: There are some people in this world, you would not love to have a bigger voice and other things in this world, you don`t necessarily want to show to everyone and that is where this job gets a little bit tough, I would imagine.\par \par \uc2 NEAL MOHAN: Whenever a decision comes up to me, it`s typically a tradeoff between two bad choices, otherwise, the decision would have been made somewhere else in the organization.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Yes.\par \par \uc2 NEAL MOHAN: And my number one responsibility is keeping our ecosystem of creators, viewers, all of our partners safe on \uc2 YouTube\uc2  and I put that above anything else that we do.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Including profit.\par \par \uc2 NEAL MOHAN: That is the north star by which we govern all of our actions.\par \par \uc2 TONY 