t to dissolve my salt and sugar. Let that steep. It`s almost like you`re making a mint syrup like a mint tea.\par \par \uc2 The next step is to cut up my cucumber and put it in my blender. So I`m using a large seedless cucumber. You can use a cucumber with seeds, but I would cut it down the middle and scrape out the seeds. So I`m going to move this to my blender.\par \par \uc2 I`m going to add some fresh ginger. It adds a little bit of spice, a little bit of heat, and doing just chopped ginger unpeeled. I`m also going to do some lime juice and the last ingredient I`m going to do is lime zest. I really love citrus zest. You can use lemon zest if you don`t have limes.\par \par \uc2 And in my blender now I`m going to add one cup of room temperature water. Everything is in my blender right now. I`m going to blend it to a fine pulp and then pass it through the strainer.\par \par \uc2 I`m going to go ahead and put some fresh mint leaves in my glass. I chilled my glass a little bit, put some ice in it because I want this to be really cold. It`s been hot this summer.\par \par \uc2 I`m going to pour my agua fresca in here. I`m going to start with about a tablespoon of simple syrup. I`ll give it a stir.\par \par \uc2 That`s really good. It`s so refreshing. It`s so light.\par \par \uc2 And that`s it. You have a drink of under 10 minutes. If you want to add a shot of alcohol to this, I think it would be really good with vodka or gin, but you know the choice is yours.\par \par \uc2 (End VT)\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: I`m going to choose -- I`m going to choose a shot of alcohol. I love that one.\par \par \uc2 Next Thursday, another recipe for you, a delicious salmon dish with a Korean flair. I will definitely be making that as well.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: All right, up next, CBS MORNINGS Deals has something that might help make your day a little bit brighter. Gayle Bass will show us these candles and how you can get them for more than 50 percent off the retail price.\par 