ON: Gayle mentioned acupuncture and of course, there`s treatment if you`re seen by a doctor. Is there anything else you might recommend?\par \par \uc2 DR. BABAK AZIZZADEH: Acupuncture, actually, without electrical stimulation is fantastic.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Okay.\par \par \uc2 DR. BABAK AZIZZADEH: There aren`t a lot of Western studies looking at it, but it`s been used for a millennia. Long term, if patients do not get recovery, we`ve pioneered surgeries and treatments with Botox, physiotherapy, and surgeries that can actually help patients really recover well.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Do you find most women don`t talk about this, that they`re suffering in silence with it?\par \par \uc2 DR. BABAK AZIZZADEH: Huge, because it`s embarrassing, right? And people go -- they stop smiling and they get depressed because smiling, you know, releases endorphins and makes us happy. And when you stop smiling, you go down and go into major psychosocial issues.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Dr. Babak Azizzadeh, thank you so much for joining us.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: And you`re flying right back to Los Angeles.\par \par \uc2 DR. BABAK AZIZZADEH: No, I have one day in New York.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: All right. Okay.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: All right.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: All right, enjoy yourself.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Yes.\par \par \uc2 DR. BABAK AZIZZADEH: I can`t come here and leave right away.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: We will be right back.\par \par \uc2 (ANNOUNCEMENTS)\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Coming up, our conversation with actor, Simon Pegg about his role in the new "Mission Impossible" movie, plus a "Talk of the Table" to remember, a textbook Florida story for you, it involves the phrase`s longest ever and python.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Well, you`re a Florida boy, you could say it. You can talk about Florida.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Oh, yes.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: I 