E: Sara Bareilles, "Into the Woods."\par \par \uc2 (Clip from "Kimberly Akimbo.")\par \par \uc2 LEA MICHELE: Victoria Clark, "Kimberly Akimbo."\par \par \uc2 (Clip from "& Juliet.")\par \par \uc2 LEA MICHELE: Lorna Courtney, "& Juliet."\par \par \uc2 (Clip from "Parade.")\par \par \uc2 LEA MICHELE: And Micaela Diamond, "Parade."\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Wow, Micaela Diamond, just 23 years old.\par \par \uc2 LEA MICHELE: I know. I was with her last night.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: You were.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: That was one of the votes.\par \par \uc2 LEA MICHELE: I was so excited.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Lovely.\par \par \uc2 MYLES FROST: Oh, yes. Oh, yes.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: All right, Myles, what`s up next?\par \par \uc2 (Clip from "Ain`t No Mo.`")\par \par \uc2 MYLES FROST: Let`s do it. The nominees for Best Play are --\par \par \uc2 (Clip from "Between Riverside and Crazy.`")\par \par \uc2 MYLES FROST: "Between Riverside and Crazy."\par \par \uc2 (Clip from "Cost of Living.")\par \par \uc2 MYLES FROST: "Cost of Living."\par \par \uc2 (Clip from "Fat Ham.")\par \par \uc2 MYLES FROST: "Fat Ham."\par \par \uc2 (Clip from "Leopoldstadt."\par \par \uc2 MYLES FROST: And "Leopoldstadt."\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Great. "Fat Ham." "Fat Ham" was on there.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: So what do you look for best performers? What do you look for when it comes to selecting some of your favorites?\par \par \uc2 LEA MICHELE: Oh, as far as like, who should be the nominees?\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Yes.\par \par \uc2 LEA MICHELE: Oh, my. I just -- everyone is so -- listen, on Broadway, we perform. We do eight shows a week. It`s so hard going on stage every single night, everyone that is working right now in theater is just doing an incredible job.\par \par \uc2 MYLES FROST: No, they are, and sustainability is one of the biggest things, you know keeping up with your health, so I commend anybody that does theater in general especially Broadway.\par \par \uc2 LEA MICHELE: Exactly.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: No doubt.\par \par \uc2 MYLES FROST: You know, and yes, just being deep into the role, you know being focused and really being able to accurately just share the story and you know connect with the -- sorry, Tony. I am so sorry.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: He is not talking about you, Tony.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: I was going to say, I like seeing my name in lights. It is lovely.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: All right, so let`s get to our final category.\par \par \uc2 MYLES FROST: Oh yes\par \par \uc2 LEA MICHELE: All right. Finally, the nominees for Best Musical are --\par \par \uc2 (Clip from (& Juliet.")\par \par \uc2 LEA MICHELE: "& Juliet."\par \par \uc2 (Clip from "Kimberly Akimbo.")\par \par \uc2 LEA MICHELE: "Kimberly Akimbo."\par \par \uc2 (Clip from "New York, New York.")\par \par \uc2 LEA MICHELE: "New York, New York."\par \par \uc2 (Clip from "Shucked.")\par \par \uc2 LEA MICHELE: "Shucked."\par \par \uc2 (Clip from "Some Like It Hot.")\par \par \uc2 LEA MICHELE: And "Some Like It Hot."\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: I love a good musical. I look at that list, I want to come. I`m definitely going to see you Lea before you leave in September.\par \par \uc2 LEA MICHELE: Please.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: But I remember being in the audience for "Spring Awakened."\par \par \uc2 LEA MICHELE: I know.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: And your parents were seated behind me. They were saying, "That`s my daughter. That`s my daughter." And I was so excited for you and for them just watching you on stage.\par \par \uc2 You`ve always done musicals. Would you ever think about doing a play?\par \par \uc2 LEA MICHELE: Oh yes. After singing all of these songs every single night, a play would be wonderful, but no, I mean, it`s hard in other aspects. That would be so fun, of course.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: But what does Broadway mean to you? To be on stage eight shows a week?\par \par \uc2 LEA MICHELE: Broadway is my life. I started working on Broadway when I was eight years old. I did my first Broadway show, "Les Mis." This has, you know, been the most incredible journey in life being able to be on Broadway and be in shows.\par \par \uc2 I`ve worked with a lot of people that were nominated today and to be in the show now that like you said, I`ve been dreaming of my whole life is so wild and unbelievable.\par \par \uc2 And to be doing it as a mom, I`m going to go pick my son up from school in a little while, so --\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: I know, back then you weren`t married.\par \par \uc2 MYLES FROST: That`s right.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: You didn`t have children.\par \par \uc2 LEA MICHELE: I know.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: And now, you`re a mom and you`re married.\par \par \uc2 LEA MICHELE: I know. Yes, and doing the show, so it`s really --\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: You are officially a grown ass woman.\par \par \uc2 LEA MICHELE: Well, you can say it.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Officially. Awesome.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Myles --\par \par \uc2 MYLES FROST: Yes.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: You had to walk away from "MJ."\par \par \uc2 MYLES FROST: Oh, yes.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: What is it like walking away from such an iconic role that you were appreciated for?\par \par \uc2 MYLES FROST: The positivity and the joy and, you know, just the love that I received, that we all received from, you know, from this musical was so beautiful. And knowing that, you know, the family was happy with it, and the fans were happy with it.\par \par \uc2 You know, the fans are ride or die for Michael. They -- you know --\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: No doubt.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes, they are.\par \par \uc2 MYLES FROST: They take him so seriously. And I love that and to know that they were satisfied and enjoyed it and enjoyed my rendition of it. You know, I try to -- I don`t try to impersonate anybody, I try to tell his story through my lens. You know, that`s what I`m good at