ar \par \uc2 ED O`KEEFE: This civil case is set to go to trial in October, setting up an unprecedented legal and political situation for the former President who of course is running again, and the various legal issues facing Trump, plus those separate legal issues facing President Biden over the handling of classified documents are just the latest reminders, Gayle, that we`ve never seen anything quite like this before.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: I know, how many times do we have to say that phrase when we`re talking about former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on many things.\par \par \uc2 And speaking of the former President, he is getting some new competition in the race for the presidency. I hear an announcement came from NH, who is that, Ed O`Keefe? That`s a clue.\par \par \uc2 ED O`KEEFE: Gayle, two South Carolina Republicans familiar with the plans tell CBS News that former South Carolina Governor and \uc2 UN\uc2  Ambassador, Nikki Haley is set to announce her presidential run in mid-February. She would be the first Republican presidential candidate to join the fray since former President Trump did so last year. Game on.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: All right, here we go. Thank you, Ed. Always good to see you.\par \par \uc2 Coming up, a change that could force hundreds of thousands of Americans to stop working from home.\par \par \uc2 And if you are heading out the door, guess what? You don`t need to miss this show. Catch the top interviews and pieces from this morning on our podcast. How do you do that? You just search for \uc2 CBS\uc2  MORNINGS On The Go on your favorite podcast app, or you can scan the QR code on the screen to start following us.\par \par \uc2 We hope you do that. You`re watching CBS MORNINGS. We`ll be right back.\par \par \uc2 (ANNOUNCEMENTS)\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Millions of Americans have been working from home during this pandemic, but now the COVID restrictions are disappearing so many large employers are saying to their employees, "