 with those of his own trading firm, \uc2 Alameda Research\uc2 , a company he characterized yesterday as one of FTX`s customers.\par \par \uc2 SAM BANKMAN-FRIED: I was frankly surprised by how big Alameda`s position was, which points to another failure of oversight on my part. I wasn`t trying to commingled funds.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: When FTX customers heard reports that billions of their funds were being moved to Bankman-Fried`s own trading firm, the run on withdrawals bankrupted the company, leaving millions of customers emptyhanded.\par \par \uc2 He now could face multiple securities fraud charges.\par \par \uc2 SAM BANKMAN-FRIED: One unbelievably important area that we completely failed on and that was risk. That was risk management that was you know, customer position risk.\par \par \uc2 SASHA HODDER (Attorney): It`s absolutely a foolish move.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Attorney Sasha Hodder, who specializes in crypto law says that admission could be yet another big risk on Bankman-Fried`s part.\par \par \uc2 SASHA HODDER: We have the Fifth Amendment right against self-incrimination for a reason, and I think every public statement he is making here is going to be used against him in the Court of law.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: But Wednesday, Bankman-Fried was more focused on apologizing than any personal legal concerns.\par \par \uc2 SAM BANKMAN-FRIED: There`s going to be a time and a place for me to sort of think about myself and my own future, but I don`t think this is it.\par \par \uc2 (End VT)\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Our legal expert you heard there, Sasha Hodder added, it is possible that Bankman-Fried will be arrested once he steps back on US soil from the Bahamas. He is set to return in February to face the \uc2 Texas Securities Board\uc2  that is looking into FTX collapse.\par \par \uc2 Hodder also likened his alleged fraud to that of Bernie Madoff. You`ll recall Bernie Madoff was sentenced to 150 years behind bars.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Oh, wow.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: That`s a lot to prepare for.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: How do you not knowingly do what he did?\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: That`s the question.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: With the expertise that he has?\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: The legal authorities there, you know, did he knowingly do this? Did he engineer this? Or was he unaware that this was happening? But the allegations are strong.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Yes. His lawyers, he said in the interview that they were not recommending that he talked like he did yesterday. So, it is very interesting to hear him go public in this way.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: He has been doing it quite a bit. He has actually been talking a lot.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: I`m not sure if that`s a good strategy.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: I don`t think he`s lawyers say it`s not, so.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes, but if I`m an investor, I want to hear from him because, dude, where`s my money?\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: He is apologetic, but you`re right.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: I don`t need an apology.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Apology doesn`t give me my money.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Apology doesn`t pay the bills.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Very correct, Gayle, it does not pay the bills. That is true. That is true.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: It does not. Coming up, Prince William and Kate visit the US to promote their environmental goals while the Prince`s godmother is accused of racism back in the UK. That story after the break.\par \par \uc2 We`ll be right back.\par \par \uc2 (ANNOUNCEMENTS)\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: The new Prince and Princess of Wales are making their first Royal Visit to the US since Queen Elizabeth died back in September.\par \par \uc2 William and Kate are in Boston right now to award their Earthshot Prize, rewarding efforts to fight climate change. President Biden plans to meet with them tomorrow. However, a gaffe by a member of the Royal household in the UK is now overshadowing their visit.\par \par \uc2 Senior national and environmental correspondent, that`s Ben Tracy is in Boston with more on the story.\par \par \uc2 Ben, good morning, do tell.\par \par \uc2 BEN TRACY: Gayle, good morning.\par \par \uc2 So, this trip has been carefully designed to focus on the Prince and Princess` environmental work and not the oftentimes dysfunctional Royal family, but even before the Royal couple touched down here in Boston on Wednesday, they were dealing with yet another problem at the Palace.\par \par \uc2 (Begin VT)\par \par \uc2 BEN TRACY: If you want to make sure people know you`re here to focus on the environment, you might as well start by helping Boston City Hall go green.\par \par \uc2 A crowd braved the cold and rain to offer William and Kate a Royal welcome.\par \par \uc2 PRINCE WILLIAM (Prince of Wales): Katherine and I are absolutely delighted to be with you today.\par \par \uc2 BEN TRACY: As the Prince told them what inspired their trip.\par \par \uc2 PRINCE WILLIAM: Sixty years ago, President John F. Kennedy`s moonshot speech laid down a challenge to American innovation and ingenuity that inspired me to launch Earthshot Prize.\par \par \uc2 MAN: We certainly have Royalty in the house tonight.\par \par \uc2 BEN TRACY: The couple then took in a Celtics game in President Kennedy`s hometown. The arena floor thankfully already color compliant.\par \par \uc2 These tightly choreographed visit is designed to show a more streamlined and modern monarchy following the Queen`s death, which put William next in line to the throne.\par \par \uc2 This is not only his first US visit in eight years, but also the first since his estranged brother, Harry ditched his Royal duties for life in California with his wife, Meghan, the Duchess of Sussex.\par \par \uc2 ROYA NIKKHAH: This is a really important few days for the Wales` to get their message over about what the Royal family is for.\par \par \uc2 BEN TRACY: But just before the Wales has landed in Boston, they had to respond to yet another Royal scandal.\par \par \uc2 Lady Susan Hussey, who served as the late Queen`s Lady in Waiting for 60 years and is also Prince William`s godmother, resigned after making apparently racist remarks at a Palace event, including asking a prominent Black British advocate for domestic abuse survivors, what part of Africa she is from?\par \par \uc2 WOMAN: There was question after question about, "No, no, no. Where are you really from? What country are you from? What`s your nationality? Where do your people come from?"\par \par \uc2 BEN TRACY: Kensington Palace issued a statement from the Wales` calling the comments unacceptable and saying "It is right the individual has stepped aside."\par \par \uc2 ROYA NIKKHAH: It is not helpful for the start of this trip and I think they`ll try very hard now to move the conversation on over the next few days.\par \par \uc2 (End VT)\par \par \uc2 BEN TRACY: So yes, after all of that, the Prince and Princess of Wales will now try to shift the focus back to their Earthshot Prize here in Boston. They`re going to meet with some climate entrepreneurs today, and then they hold this big-star studded event on Friday night where they`re going to hand out five prizes worth more than a million dollars each to folks who are trying to tackle the climate crisis -- Tony.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: That`s an important issue, Ben. Thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 But back to the less important issues, you know, how important was that basketball game to the Prince and Princess?\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Yes. Did you see him staring at their basketball?\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: There is all that there`s a picture of them online, whether they`re like, it is a basket-- what is this?\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: What is this?\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: People are very glad though that they are here. They`re getting a warm welcome in Boston.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: For sure.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: And I think that`s nice.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: And they`re doing something good.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes. I think that`s a nice thing.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Yes, and because everything happens at once, we`ve got more Royal news coming up in "What to Watch."\par \par \uc2 Up next, Vlad Duthiers has got the stories you`ll be talking about today, including a Netflix trailer that just dropped featuring another pair of Royals. We`ll show you which ones.\par \par \uc2 But first, it is 7:44. Time to check your local weather.\par \par \uc2 (LOCAL WEATHER)\par \par \uc2 (ANNOUNCEMENTS)\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Time now for "What to Watch."\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Oh, I just -- all right, I heard "Boogey Wonderland."\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: I love that song.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Better run, we`re going to get a camera on you, Shawna.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: We saw you dancing.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Shawna, our executive producer was grooving. Everybody grooving to "Boogey Wonderland."\par \par \uc2 All right, so let`s talk about -- we already spoke about what is happening in Boston, right?\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: We know the Prince and Princess are in Boston. Well, the first trailer for \uc2 Prince Harry\uc2  and Meghan`s Netflix docuseries dropped just a short time ago. It is called "Harry and Meghan." Watch this.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: All right.\par \par \uc2 (Clip from "Harry and Meghan.")\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: I see your visit to Boston and raise you one docuseries.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: I see that is a very good trailer. I can`t wait to see it.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: What do we think is going on there?\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: I think it is great.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: What do we think? I mean, there`s --\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: What do you mean? What do you mean?\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: There is a lot of subtext in the images that they are showing.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: For sure.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: I don`t any subtext at all. Please tell me what is happening.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Well, I mean, you see her in moments of distress, right? Looking at her phone, for whatever reason. You see her -- you see, the Prince and Princess of Wales, in a very sort of not flattering shot.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: It wasn`t a warm photo.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: It was not. Look at these photos --\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: But they are not looking at Harry Meghan. They`re looking at whatever is going on. But I think --\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: But the selection of the photo they chose for the trailer is what you`re saying.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: You`re right. That is very --\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Editing.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: That`s a very conscious choice. But I thought Meghan summed it up well, when she said, "Should we be the ones that get to tell our story."\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: When the stakes are so high.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Because everybody else has been telling their story.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Everybody has been telling it, and now you get to hear from them what their story is. I think it`s great.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Oh, I see -- I see that shot you`re talking about. Okay. My eyes are opened in a new way here.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Yes.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: That was very intense.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: It looks very intense.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: And deliberate. And deliberate.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: And deliberate. And do we think it`s a coincidence that they dropped it today when -- or it is a coincidence?\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: When does it start? When does it start?\par \par \uc2 TON