y when I was postpartum, you know, physically repairing myself. My mantra was forward is a pace. There were some days that it was like --\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Forward is a pace.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: I like that.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ARZON: I am just going to take the next step and the next step. So for folks who are in the beginning of their wellness journey, feeling overwhelmed or even paralyzed by the fear of starting something new, start with one, one intentional choice that is going to make today better.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: And I love that you say don`t wait till January, do it now.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Do it now.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ARZON: Do it now. Later becomes never.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: When people tune in to you, you get them going.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: She`s a beast.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: You gave us a mantra, but --\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: She is a beast.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: What gets you going? Do you have any songs that you can recommend for people to add to the playlist?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ARZON: Oh, my gosh. There are so many.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Okay.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Just one.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ARZON: I have Bad Bunny on repeat right now.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Okay.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ARZON: Listen, my playlist right now is like a little Taylor Swift, of course, we`ve got Mariah Carey. But it`s been Bad Bunny since summer.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Bad Bunny.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ARZON: Yes. But Athena knows how drop it like --\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: You know, it is funny when we were watching the bikes. Tony goes, but they`re really going somewhere. I go, you you`re going somewhere on the Peloton, too.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ARZON: Yes. Well, it goes everywhere.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Well, I was trying to explain, it`s a stationary bike. But --\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: I know, but you are going somewhere.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Well, you are physically going -- I mean, in a sense that you`re transforming yourself, right?\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Yes.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ARZON: It`s an immersive experience connected with music and community. It`s absolutely visceral. Obviously, I`m biased, but I really see lives change every day. We`re not only adding years to people`s lives, but life to their years.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: That`s awesome.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: But you do get on and get off at the very same point. That`s all I am saying. Robin Arzon, thank you very much. We appreciate you being here.\par \par \uc2 Coming up, if you haven`t booked that vacation for next year, we`ve got someone who can help. "Conde Nast Traveler" is revealing its best destinations in 2023. That`s going somewhere.\par \par \uc2 We`ll be right back.\par \par \uc2 (ANNOUNCEMENTS)\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: In case you missed this week`s \uc2 CBS\uc2  MORNINGS Deals on Tuesday, we showed you three items that could help make your holiday season a little easier and better all at exclusive low prices.\par \par \uc2 The MASINGO karaoke machine might help spice up your Holiday gathering with some musical entertainment like when Gayle sings here on the set, and it is available at more than 30 percent off retail price.\par \par \uc2 To start shopping now, scan the QR code on your screen right now, or you can visit CBSDeals.com.\par \par \uc2 Your local news is coming up next.\par \par \uc2 (LOCAL NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (LOCAL WEATHER)\par \par \uc2 (ANNOUNCEMENTS)\par \par \uc2 *************************************************************************** ** (08:30 AM, EDT)\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Welcome back to CBS MORNINGS.\par \par \uc2 It is time to bring you some of the stories that are the "Talk of the Table" because we have a table and like Gayle says, we be talking.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: We be talking.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: All right, Tony what have you got?\par \par 