h.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Quickly coming out of the water and sort of showing its teeth. She is known to the scientists in the area, the shark is, as Queen Nikki.\par \par \uc2 Ramsey, she is an oceanographer. She laughed off the incident and hopped into the water to dive with other sharks. Researchers think the murky water it may have caused the shark to rear its head to check her out.\par \par \uc2 I`ve been trying to interview her for years. She`s got an incredible --\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Check her out.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: She is always diving with these sharks.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: I hope she talks to you.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Yes. I really want to talk to her.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Let us talk about Larry the Cat.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: All right, let`s talk about Larry the Cat.\par \par \uc2 Rishi Sunak became Britain`s new Prime Minister this week. Many people were more interested in another resident of 10 Downing Street. We`re all of course talking about this guy.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: You know about this, Gayle?\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes, I do.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Larry the Cat.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: I like this.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: The little guy. There he is.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: He was there when Sunak talked to reporters outside the Prime Minister`s residence. This is a big week for Larry because he has officially outlasted four heads of government. Then Prime Minister David Cameron rescued the stray tabby in 2011 after his children begged him to.\par \par \uc2 Larry has lived there longer than Cameron, Theresa May, Boris Johnson, and Liz Truss.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: I saw Larry with a little podium.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Larry has got a name.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: He is the Chief Mouser to the Cabinet Office.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Chief Mouser -- there is an official portrait as well we just saw there.\par \par 