c2 GAYLE KING: Okay.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: There`s times when we look at each other and we see the fatigue, but we turn the switch on; one, because we appreciate the job; and two, because the viewer is sitting there waiting. But to us, your family and that`s why we left that seat open for you.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Yes.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Cheers.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Cheers.\par \par \uc2 (End VT)\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: That was a lovely afternoon, Nate Burleson. We all walked out of there drooling about your house saying, "We want to stay here." You are clearly the host with the most.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Well, thank you, I appreciate that and I appreciate you guys doing this.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: You and Mrs. Burleson, you and Mrs. Burleson.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Yes. Shout out to my wife. Shout out to my wife.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: You and Mrs. Burleson. That`s right.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: You know, I know this is a celebration, but I couldn`t help but to get emotional. We do have a great job and we have so much fun and there is so much love, not just with us, but also everybody else behind the scenes.\par \par \uc2 So, I want to say thank you to the team, the \uc2 CBS\uc2  family.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Yes, absolutely. I second that. I third that. You fourth that.\par \par \uc2 I`ve got one more bit of news that I want to get to before we go to break.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Oh.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Speaking of love, another moment from the meal that we want to share with our viewers something Vlad revealed.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: This is good.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Roll it.\par \par \uc2 (Begin VT)\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: So, I have a personal milestone. You know I got married during the pandemic, which was incredible, which was a milestone in of itself because I had never thought this would happen and now, we are having a baby, and it is a baby girl.\par \par