es an interview with Meghan`s friend -- they`re very good friends -- Serena Williams.\par \par \uc2 It`s her first in-depth interviews since announcing her plans to retire from tennis. The two women discuss everything from their careers to motherhood, including a brush with danger.\par \par \uc2 (Begin VT)\par \par \uc2 JAMIE YUCCAS: It was just minutes after this 2019 speech in South Africa that \uc2 Meghan Markle\uc2  says she and \uc2 Prince Harry\uc2  learned about a frightening incident involving their son Archie who was traveling with them at the time.\par \par \uc2 MEGHAN MARKLE\uc2  (Duchess of Sussex): We finished the engagement; we get in the car and they say there`s been a fire at the residence. What?\par \par \uc2 There has been a fire in the baby`s room. What?\par \par \uc2 JAMIE YUCCAS: Meghan shared the story with Serena Williams during her podcast, "Archetypes." The Duchess said the baby was thankfully with his nanny at the time.\par \par \uc2 MEGHAN MARKLE\uc2 : Her instinct was just like, let me just bring him with me before I put him down. In that amount of time that she went downstairs.\par \par \uc2 SERENA WILLIAMS (Professional tennis player): Oh my God.\par \par \uc2 MEGHAN MARKLE\uc2 : The heater in the nursery caught on fire. There was no smoke detector. Someone happened to just smell smoke down the hallway, went in, fire extinguished. He was supposed to be sleeping in there.\par \par \uc2 JAMIE YUCCAS: Despite the close call, Meghan says, she and \uc2 Prince Harry\uc2  still had a carry on with their Royal duties.\par \par \uc2 MEGHAN MARKLE\uc2 : Everyone is in tears, everyone is shaken. And what did we have to do? Go out and do another official engagement. I said, "This doesn`t make any sense." Can you just --\par \par \uc2 SERENA WILLIAMS: How did you not bring him?\par \par \uc2 MEGHAN MARKLE\uc2 : I was like, "Can you just tell people what happened?" And so much I think optically, the focus ends up being on how it looks instead of how 