ce December, the number of infected patients here nearly tripled.\par \par \uc2 Out of 286 COVID patients at this hospital, only 15 are vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 DR. ANDREW SCHLACHTER: Are you coughing?\par \par \uc2 PAMELA MAPLES (COVID patient): A little.\par \par \uc2 CARTER EVANS: Pamela Maples avoided the vaccine because she thought it was more dangerous than COVID.\par \par \uc2 Were you concerned about COVID before?\par \par \uc2 When she tested positive last month, she was in the hospital eight days later.\par \par \uc2 PAMELA MAPLES: I had no clue it would be like this.\par \par \uc2 CARTER EVANS: What did you think it might be?\par \par \uc2 PAMELA MAPLES: Oh, like it`s a flu. It`s a regular old flu. That`s what everybody kept telling me.\par \par \uc2 CARTER EVANS: It`s a story nurse Kristin Sollars hears too often.\par \par \uc2 KRISTIN SOLLARS: There`s a lot of anger about the community not wanting to take care of themselves and asking for us to pick up that slack when they become critically ill. And other days, it is really profound sadness, because we have the saddest stories you`ve ever heard in your life.\par \par \uc2 CARTER EVANS: And after weeks in the hospital, Pamela Maples is now begging others to get the shot.\par \par \uc2 PAMELA MAPLES: Take the vaccine. It`s very, very important.\par \par \uc2 (End VT)\par \par \uc2 CARTER EVANS: Now Pam`s ex-husband was also in the here being treated for COVID, but he died last week. And after everything this family has been through, Pam says there are still some close friends and family members that will not get the vaccine -- Gayle.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: I don`t know what more people need to see, but thank you very much, Carter. We have to just keep telling this story. Thanks a lot.\par \par \uc2 Jury selection begins this morning in the Federal trial of three fired Minneapolis Police Officers facing civil rights charges in the George Floyd case.\par \par \uc2 Thomas Lane, J. Alexander Kueng, and Tou Thao were all at the scene when Derek Chauvin killed Floyd by kneeling on his neck for more than nine minutes -- nine minutes and 29 seconds.\par \par \uc2 Chauvin was convicted of murder in a separate state trial last spring. Now, he has pleaded guilty to one of the Federal charges. Mola Lenghi is at the Federal Courthouse in St. Paul where the other three men will now go on trial.\par \par \uc2 (Begin VT)\par \par \uc2 MAN: We`re back in session and on the record.\par \par \uc2 MOLA LENGHI: Unlike the trial last spring where court cameras captured Derek Chauvin as prosecutors successfully made their case, this trial won`t be broadcast.\par \par \uc2 Former Minneapolis Police Officers Thomas Lane, J. Alexander Kueng, and Tou Thao are charged with willfully depriving George Floyd of his civil rights.\par \par \uc2 Attorney and legal analyst Joe Tamburino.\par \par \uc2 What is the defense`s argument here?\par \par \uc2 JOE TAMBURINO (Attorney and legal analyst): The defense`s argument is twofold. Number one, that they did not willfully try to violate the rights of Mr. Floyd. And secondly, that they had no part in what Mr. Chauvin was doing.\par \par \uc2 MOLA LENGHI: Video of the deadly 2020 encounter shows Lane, Kueng, and Thao also at the scene as Chauvin kneels on Floyd`s neck. Lane and Kueng had been on the force for less than a week.\par \par \uc2 At the heart of this case is whether or not the defendants could and should have tried to stop Chauvin.\par \par \uc2 JOE TAMBURINO: In Minnesota, the only person that has to render any aid would be the Good Samaritan laws, but they don`t apply to police officers.\par \par \uc2 MAN: I can`t breathe.\par \par \uc2 CROWD: I can`t breathe.\par \par \uc2 MOLA LENGHI: In Minnesota, the troubled relationship between police and the community goes beyond the death of George Floyd. Just last month, former Brooklyn Center Police Officer Kim Potter was convicted of manslaughter in the shooting death of Daunte Wright.\par \par 